[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two matte ceramic plates set on an aged oak wood tabletop, captured at a 3/4 overhead angle (40°). The dish is centered to allow for circular cropping. Shallow depth of field keeps the foreground plate sharp, while the second plate is slightly out of focus in the background. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window to the left, creating subtle shadows and highlights on the tomato sauce. The shakshuka consists of a vibrant red, chunky tomato and chickpea base with ribbons of wilted, bright green spinach throughout. Two large eggs are nestled into the sauce per plate, with firm, opaque whites and glistening, jammy, soft-set golden yolks. A generous dollop of thick, creamy white Greek yogurt is swirled onto the side of the tomato mixture on each plate. Two halves of toasted, lightly charred whole-wheat pita bread are tucked against the side of each plate. Props include a small, rustic wooden spoon resting on the table near a stray chickpea and a few tiny spinach fragments. The scene reflects a home-cooked, warm meal. There is a small, natural sauce drip on the rim of the plate and an imperfect swirl of yogurt. The atmosphere is cozy, golden-hour, and authentic. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
  }
]
